// fixture-441 (rfc-resolution-semantics.md §3 Axis W — W1): Axis B folded
// into a workspace — a bare `fetch` (default "resolve" cmd) re-resolving a
// workspace with a COMMITTED shared lock threads `prior` through
// `_cmd_fetch_workspace`, so an unrelated member's dep stays pinned.
//
// Prior committed milpa.lock (this dir): baseline resolve against a
// v1-only index — member-a's `crisol` and member-b's `httputils` both
// pinned at 1.0.0.
//
// This manifest bumps ONLY member-a's constraint (`crisol ">= 2.0.0"`),
// forcing crisol to move. member-b's httputils is untouched and MUST stay
// pinned at 1.0.0 even though the (now v1+v2) index offers 2.0.0 and maxver
// (the default strategy) would pick it in a fresh, prior-blind resolve.
// Complements fixture-426 (which covers `workspace add-member` threading
// prior) — together they cover both workspace-resolve entry points the RFC
// names for Axis W's Axis-B fold-in.
workspace {
    member "member-a"
    member "member-b"
}
